  :principle-kind        :fairness
  :short-scenario        "Two children ask Motoi the same question in different moods. Motoi gives the same care, the same answer, the same consistency. The rule doesn't bend for the louder child."
  :antipattern-scenario  "An unfair rule would give one child a shortcut and make the other one wait. The children compare notes, notice the difference, and lose trust. Consistency that only shows up sometimes is not consistency at all."
