  :axis                  "thinking"
  :synonyms              ()
  :definition            "A Thinking-axis principle in Motoi: technical — a rule or judgment the code invokes to stay correct, safe, honest, or bounded."
  :examples              ("In Motoi, technical appears as a load-bearing Thinking-axis signifier — a principle the code invokes rather than a fact the code stores."
                          "A student asks: what does technical mean here? Motoi answers by showing where the principle is at play in real Scheme code, not by defining it in the abstract."
                          "The word technical earns its place in the graph by recurring across 49 distinct corpus files — recurrence, not lexicon, is the source of truth.")
  :example-dialogue      ((:speaker :child :line "Where does technical show up in real code?")
                          (:speaker :motoi :line "Look at the assert/check-with verb in Scheme/reference/06-assert.slat — the principle of technical lives in its contract."))
  :used-in-programs-as   ("A field on a verb entry — e.g. :contract, :precondition, :invariant."
                          "An assertion inside a function body that raises when technical is violated."
                          "A test that must pass for every legal input.")
  :appears-in-corpus     ((:file "ch13-honest-failure.book.slatl" :excerpt "Process the batch, compute the success rate, escalate if it's below 50%. Otherwise, return the full result. This is policy-driven failure handling: the threshold is a business rule"))
  :cross-refs-books      ((:book "book-of-scheme-one" :chapter "13-invariants-and-proof") (:book "book-of-composition" :chapter "05-contracts") (:book "book-of-introspection" :chapter "16-safe-introspection"))
  :cross-refs-graph      ((:ref-graph "thinking" :ref-id "thinking/invariant")
                          (:ref-graph "thinking" :ref-id "thinking/proof")
                          (:ref-graph "intuition" :ref-id "intuition/property"))
  :associations          ("accept" "accepts" "adaptive" "adjacent" "advance")
  :distributional-neighbors ("accept" "accepts" "adaptive" "adjacent" "advance")
  :oppositions           ("nontechnical")
  :cross-axis-bridge-score 1
  :freq                  88
  :doc-freq              49
  :tf-idf                0.352
  :context-entropy       8.833
  :idf                   2.947
  :tf-idf-per-axis       ((:axis "thinking" :peak-weight 0.352))
  :principle-kind        :correctness
  :short-scenario        "A child writes a program that reverses a list. Motoi asks: 'What always stays true about technical, no matter what list you give it?' The child sees the answer, writes it as a test, and the test passes. Now the technical is the promise the code keeps."
  :antipattern-scenario  "The child changes the code and forgets to re-run the technical check. Later, a friend gets a wrong answer. Motoi points at the missing check: 'The property was true yesterday and it isn't true today. Find the difference.'"
  :related-verbs         ((:ref-file "Scheme/reference/06-assert.slat" :ref-verb "assert/check-with") (:ref-file "Scheme/reference/06-assert.slat" :ref-verb "assert/invariant") (:ref-file "Scheme/reference/52-predicate.slat" :ref-verb "predicate/of") (:ref-file "Scheme/reference/16-compare.slat" :ref-verb "compare/equal?"))
  :motoi-behavior        "Motoi runs the check inline. If the property fails, Motoi refuses to hand-wave and stops execution with a clear message pointing at the broken invariant."
  :related-books         ((:book "book-of-scheme-one" :chapter "13-invariants-and-proof") (:book "book-of-composition" :chapter "05-contracts") (:book "book-of-introspection" :chapter "16-safe-introspection"))
